# Spec Kit machine-local pointer — REQUIRED at root level (Spec Kit Standard Rev C, P3).
# This line is on `main` deliberately, and `main` is the branch that most needs it: it carries
# no `.specify/` scaffold, so it carries no `.specify/.gitignore` either. A `.specify/feature.json`
# left on disk by a feature branch SURVIVES the switch to `main` (checkout never deletes untracked
# files) and, without this line, is untracked AND unignored — one `git add -A` in a records-only
# session commits another machine's feature pointer. Reproduced in this repo on 2026-08-08 before
# adding it: on `main`, `git check-ignore` did not match and `git add -An` reported
# `add '.specify/feature.json'`. Same holds after `git branch -D` of a rejected branch.
.specify/feature.json
